A third case of the same defect, found after this was filed, for whoever plans or builds it: the mirror image of the Sack.

**A base Ticketed made Radiant in place still crumbles from its base face's Brittle 3.** S #9 Ticketed is the only card whose base face prints Brittle and whose Radiant face prints none. A base Ticketed is played and gets `BrittleCounter { count: 3, printed: Some(true) }`. S #110 iKwzki's Duo makes it Radiant at the start of its controller's next turn. The count keeps ticking, 2 then 1 then 0, and the Radiant Ticketed is destroyed (`crumbled`).

- R1875001: "The Radiant face has no Brittle, so it holds until it is removed."
- `active_brittle_count` (`crates/engine/src/brittle_count.rs:27-33`) switches a printed count off only for `vanilla`, though its own doc says "A count its printed Brittle started is the card's text": a face that no longer prints Brittle is the same case.
- Starting a count on becoming Radiant (the Sack's fix above) does not fix this one. Treat a count with `printed: Some(true)` as in force only while the running face still prints Brittle (in `active_brittle_count`, beside the Vanilla test), or drop it in `make_radiant`.
- The same count survives a bounce to hand (R766), so a Ticketed made Radiant off the field and replayed would crumble too; that path is by reading, not tested.

Failing test: `ticketed_made_radiant_in_place_no_longer_crumbles` in [`crates/ai/tests/audit_cards_stinky.rs` at ca59d7a](https://github.com/Jlore-Studios/JackiOh/blob/ca59d7a/crates/ai/tests/audit_cards_stinky.rs). Its control (a Ticketed played Radiant stands through four of its controller's turns) passes; the base one made Radiant ends in the graveyard: ``R1875001: the Radiant face has no Brittle, so it holds until it is removed; it is in Graveyard { player: P1 } with 1 `crumbled` ``.

